<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gabriel García Moreno</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1821–1875</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gabriel García Moreno was twice president of Ecuador, from 1861 to 1865 and from 1869 until his assassination in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a> in 1875. A conservative Catholic, he signed a concordat with the Vatican, dedicated the country to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sacred-heart">Sacred Heart</a> and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a> a condition of citizenship, while also building roads, schools and the Quito observatory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gabriel-garcia-moreno.jpg" alt="Gabriel García Moreno" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Presidencia de la República del Ecuador · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gabriel_Garc%C3%ADa_Moreno.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
